  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study relies on a relatively small sample of 90 municipal officials within a single city, and its findings are based on self-reported survey data rather than objective measures of diplomatic outcomes.",
      "what": "This study analyzes the governance model of urban diplomacy in Tehran using a survey of 90 municipal officials, including mayors and department vice-presidents. The researchers used Likert-scale questionnaires to measure governance, urban diplomacy, and globalization, validating the relationships with Cronbach's alpha reliability scores of 76%, 83%, and 89% respectively. The analysis identified causal relationships and significant associations between urban diplomacy and governance indicators such as accountability, central consensus, international relations, and management power.",
      "why": "It establishes a empirical link between internal municipal governance structures and a megacity's capacity to conduct international urban diplomacy, identifying specific administrative traits like accountability and consensus-building that facilitate global engagement."
    }
